    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/09/puma-magnify-nitro-3-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The full-length Nitro foam is notably soft/compliant with strong impact protection and a plush ride; heel transition can feel clunky, while the forefoot feels well-cushioned and smooth.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is moderate with some rebound/bounce for easy to moderate uptempo efforts, but it is not especially snappy for faster interval work.",
        "Stability: This is a true neutral shoe; the very soft foam and narrow midfoot can feel a bit wobbly laterally, though lockdown is secure and the heel counter is moderately stiff.",
        "Durability: Outsole durability appears average with early wear on exposed areas and reported posterolateral rubber tearing around 30 miles, while midsole feel has remained consistent so far."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/07/puma-magnify-nitro-3-review-2.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The 100% PEBA NitroFoam feels highly comfortable and protective but less mushy than v2; the 40/30 mm stack and 10 mm drop give smooth heel-first landings with a pleasant forefoot feel.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is strong and the ride is distinctly bouncy; the updated foam feels more responsive and the decoupling groove makes toe-off snappier, though transitions remain on the slower side at faster paces.",
        "Stability: It is notably stable for a bouncy trainer, helped by a wide platform, rearfoot cradle/rails, secure lockdown, and a semi-structured padded heel counter; the softer exposed midfoot is the least stable area.",
        "Durability: PumaGrip is described as top-tier for traction and lasting power, but limited outsole coverage (about one-third uncovered midsole) may modestly reduce long-term lifespan."
      ]
    }
